  "why": "The statement is the local restriction problem over real or p-adic fields, with different forms for each classical family, so every local result restricted to one family, field type, or tempered/generic/non-tempered class is a case, and nothing in the record settles all families. Global automorphic period results (BPLZZ, BPCZ, BP-Chaudouard, Furusawa-Morimoto, Haan, Boisseau-Lu-Xue, Haan-Kwon) concern the global period vs L-value statement, which the bullet does not state, so they are variants; so are Ext-level analogues (Chan-Savin, Rui Chen, Qadri, Chan-Qadri), the twisted GGP pairs (Le), GSpin Bessel uniqueness, and arithmetic transfer. Post-snapshot local cases: Chen-Chen (one direction of archimedean non-tempered GL), Boisseau (local nonzero-form construction completing the archimedean GL case), Chen-Chen-Zou (basic tempered real Fourier-Jacobi metaplectic), and Pattanayak (p-adic GL Hom criterion for unitarizable representations); all unreviewed preprints by researchers in the field, so credible. Pattanayak's counterexample refutes a theorem in Gurevich's paper, not the conjecture, so object_role is null. Boisseau 2025 was counted as a local case because its abstract claims a local construction and local settlement, though its main thrust is global. Chen's thesis is unread and was scored none. No AI system appears in any event.",
